.TH QUITALL 1
.SH NAME
quitall \- kill every process and exit emu
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quitall
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Quitall
kills every process, which ends
.IR emu :
it leaves when its last Dis process does.
.PP
.IR Wm (1)
has no quit of its own, and
.B exit
only ends the shell inside it.
.SH "WHY IT EXISTS"
Measurement, rather than tidiness.
Comparing two runs of a session requires both to stop for the same reason.
Stopping them with a timer from outside compares where the timer landed as
much as anything the system did \(em which is exactly what went wrong in an
earlier version of the measurement in
.IR schedcmp (1),
where two runs appeared to do an identical amount of work and had merely been
cut off at similar points.
.PP
A recorded session that ends by running this ends at the same place every time.
Its name is all letters so that a synthetic keyboard can type it, which is how
such a recording gets made \(em see
.IR emu (1)
for
.BR INFERNO_INPUT_RECORD .
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/quitall.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR emu (1),
.IR schedcmp (1),
.IR inputtest (1)
.SH BUGS
It reads all of
.B /prog
before killing anything, because the directory changes underneath as processes
die and a partial sweep leaves the session up \(em which is the one outcome
that would make this useless.
.PP
It kills itself last, and does not report what it killed, because by then there
is nothing left to report to.
.PP
No warning, no confirmation, nothing saved.
